### 1. Executive Profile & Organizational History

The **Dalit Welfare Association (DWA)** is a non-profit, non-commercial voluntary society headquartered in rural Kurnool District, Andhra Pradesh. Formally established on **June 22, 1993**, the association operates under a non-political charter dedicated to empowering marginalized Dalit communities, Below Poverty Line (BPL) families, single women, widows, and underprivileged children.

```
Dalit Welfare Association Operational Evolution
• 1993: Official Registration under Societies Registration Act XXI of 1860 (Reg No. 384/1993).
• 2004–2012: Grassroots campaigns in adult education, solid waste management, safe drinking water, and hygiene.
• 2016–2017: First major overseas grant execution ($4,39,000 INR from Global Compassion Inc. USA) for dairy farming.
• 2020–2022: COVID-19 emergency relief distribution (₹8.32 Lakh grant from Divya Foundation).
• 2024–2025+: Women’s Banking & Entrepreneurship Program (₹33.19 Lakh FCRA grant from Grace TPTC Foundation).
```

* **Foundational Governance:** DWA is registered under the **Societies Registration Act XXI of 1860** (Society Reg No. `384/1993`) through the District Registrar of Assurances, Kurnool.
* **Core Mandate:** Under its registered bylaws, DWA operates strictly with no profit motive, forbids commercial profit sharing, prohibits political or agitational activities, and ensures that office bearers receive no salary or dividends from society funds.
* **Registered Address:** H.No. 4-84 (formerly 8/5), S.C. Colony, Parnapalli Village & Post, Bandi Atmakur Mandal, Kurnool District, Andhra Pradesh – 518523.
* **Vision:** To be a sustainable organization empowering the rural poor, economically and socially, irrespective of caste and creed.
* **Mission:** To enable the rural poor to attain sustainable growth by creating livelihood opportunities through microfinance and income-generation programs via a fair and transparent system.

