### 5. Detailed Program Architecture & Intervention Models

#### A. Women’s Banking & Entrepreneurship Development Program
This flagship 12-month intervention targets **50 rural women entrepreneurs** (prioritizing Below Poverty Line, single, and widowed women aged 25–50) in Sirivella Block (3 selected villages), Kurnool District. 

The program follows a standardized **6-Stage Operating Model** [48–53]:
1. **Livelihood Scoping:** Market research mapping local demand, value chains, and raw material availability.
2. **Beneficiary Selection:** Community meetings with Self-Help Groups (SHGs) to select 50 high-interest women.
3. **Curriculum Customization:** Developing dialect-translated workbooks covering financial literacy and trade skills.
4. **Resource Deployment:** Deploying Master Trainers for hands-on instruction.
5. **3-Phase Skill Building:**
   * *Financial Education & Digital Banking:* Household budgeting, savings, formal bank account usage, debit cards, and UPI payments.
   * *Business Planning:* Product branding, packaging, pricing, inventory management, and Udyog Aadhaar licensing.
   * *Livelihood Upgradation:* Trade-specific coaching across tailoring, livestock, and micro-retail.
6. **Monitoring & Evaluation:** Baseline and post-intervention tracking of income and savings.

```
Itemized 12-Month Project Budget Breakdown ($16,064 USD Total)
• Project Initiation Meetings (2): $135
• 2 Master Trainers Salary (6 Months): $1,620 ($135/mo per trainer)
• 2 Training Room Leases (6 Months): $324 ($27/mo per room)
• Tailoring Units (10 Sewing Machines @ $95 + Cloth/Raw Materials): $1,355
• Livestock Units (80 Baby Sheep for 20 Women @ $68 ea + 12-mo Insurance $110): $5,550
• Micro-Grocery Retail Stores (20 Shop setups @ $68 + Groceries @ $205 ea): $5,460
• Project Officer Salary (12 Months): $1,620 ($135/mo)
```

* **Target KPIs:** `+35%` revenue growth, `+25%` formal savings growth, `100%` bank accounts with debit cards, `≥60%` Udyog Aadhaar registration, and `≥50%` active UPI/digital payment adoption.
* **Funding Partner:** Supported by **Grace TPTC Foundation** via an FCRA foreign contribution grant of **₹33,19,167** in FY 2024–25.

#### B. Primary School Support & Dalit Child Education
* **Academic Outreach:** Ongoing educational drives across **10 Government Primary Schools** in Sirivella and Bandi Atmakur mandals.
* **School Supply Kits (₹1,200 per kit):** Includes 3 long notebooks, pens, pencils, erasers, sharpeners, color pencils, 1 durable school bag, and 1 new dress/uniform set.
* **Merit Scholarships:** Direct financial aid awarded annually to high-performing Dalit students to prevent dropouts.

#### C. Emergency & Seasonal Relief Initiatives
* **COVID-19 Relief (FY 2020–21):** Supported by a **₹8,32,500** grant from Divya Foundation, distributing 30 kg dry ration kits and youth happiness kits to BPL families and street children.
* **30 kg Dry Ration Package Breakdown (₹1,200 value):** Rice (₹400), Wheat flour (₹320), Moong/Toor Dal (₹100), Refined Oil (₹100), Sugar/Jaggery (₹40), Chilli powder (₹30), Turmeric (₹30), Potato (₹60), Onion (₹50), Soya chunks (₹35), Salt (₹15), and packaging/travel (₹20).

